# CHANGELOG

LEGEND:
Development version <VERSION x.x.x> - <DATE> yyyy-mm-dd - Specifies latest version, not current changes in this codebase. use UNRELEASED for the date if that is the case

Development version Alpha 0.0.1 - 2026-04-13
-----------------------------------------------
- Deployed raw framework without game with a few additions such as the save and load systems.
- Implemented save/load system and forced username creation. Username creation does not cause any network effects, it's purely metadata, but useful for all kinds of games.

Development version Alpha 0.0.1a - 2026-05-03
------------------------------------------------
- Updated helper.py with some instructions on the asset string system
- Updated config.py to be neutral when using setup
- Ensured core systems were up to snuff # they weren't

Development version Alpha 0.1.0 - 2026-06-24 
-------------------------------------------------
- Removed custom surface object to rely soley on pygame's main surface. 
- Included unused experimental files
- Added more pygame wrappers in Window.py 
- Added a mesh loader
- Added a Triangle class
- Added a basic 3D math module
- Application name is now in a local config file (this is when the developer runs setup.py)
- Changed license to MIT. GPL just wasn't open enough for me.
